cited to  see sony feature a game like bug snacks  at the ps5 reveal event  this one immediately pops with color and  has an undeniable charm from the first  moment you see it  and hear it it reminds me a bit of  cloudy with a chance of meatballs  although its gameplay is inspired by  titles such as pokemon snap and ape  escape  it's described as a first-person  adventure game with 100 different  species of bug snacks for players to  capture  my son and i can't wait to dive in  number eight returnal  my hype for returnal is based almost  solely on my love for the devs at house  mark  i think they're one of the most  under-appreciated devs in the entire  industry resogun was a ps4 launch title  that to this day is one of my favorite  games on the system  they also made nex machina super  stardust dead nation  the list just goes on and on an  absolutely insane  quality library that sometimes went  unnoticed  returnal is a departure for them though  as they pivot away from  arcade style shooters into third person  regardless these guys know what makes  good gameplay and i  fully expect fraternal to blow folks  away when it launches  hopefully the shift into a more popular  genre will bring house mark the  attention  and sales they deserve number seven  horizon forbidden west  the big time success of horizon zero  dawn made a sequel  all but inevitable i mean come on a  third person action game with a strong  lead character  unique weaponry and dinosaur mechs yes  please give me more  the devs at gorilla are incredibly  talented as they've shown over the years  with the kill zone titles but making the  move to a game like horizon was clearly  the right move  they showed they were capable of much  more by delivering an open world action  game that also had a strong story  there's no doubt expectations will be  very high for forbidden west  number six ratchet and clank rift apart  it's hard to believe ratchet is almost  20 years  old guys for the younger ones out there  who may not remember ratchet debuted on  the playstation 2 all  the way back in 2002. seriously guys  2002.  despite his age insomniac continues to  pump out games that get better  and better than the ones before it  what's kind of crazy though is this will  be the first  truly new ratchet game since into the  nexus which released on ps3 back in  2013.  ps4 did have a ratchet game back in 2016  but it was actually a remake of the  first game  which was an incredible remake by the  way rift apart is expected to have  players  jumping quickly between different worlds  thanks in large part to the ps5  super fast ssd we don't have a release  date just yet but most  expect this one to hit in early 2021  number five spider-man miles morales  this one certainly needs no introduction  after insomniac gave us the incredibly  popular spider-man game in 2018 we  already know they have what it takes to  deliver  to be honest with you guys what  surprised me most about that 2018  version  of spider-man was how good they made the  story  it's insomniac so he knew the action and  gameplay would be top-notch but the  story really blew me away  now we'll get to play as a new  spider-man with miles morales  with the huge success of spider-man into  the spider-verse and a sequel on the way  this game comes at a perfect time  playing as miles will give gamers a  chance to explore a different character  other than peter parker  and with the story being so good in the  original game i'm excited to see what  they have planned out for miles  speaking of into the spider verse we now  have confirmation that this suit will be  in the game which is incredible not only  that insomniac went the extra mile by  giving us the option to have spider-man  move  at 12 fps now normally in a video game  we want  higher frame rates not lower but this is  a special circumstance because the frame  rate  actually would then match that of the  film making it feel  even more like you're actually playing  as miles from the spider-verse flick  you do have the option of turning it off  however if it proves too distracting or  you're just not a fan of the effect  number four kana bridge of spirits look  we already know spider-man is gonna  deliver we know horizon's gonna deliver  but maybe an  under the radar title that really  excited me from the ps5 reveal event  is kana i'm not sure there was a trailer  more impressive than what we saw with  canaan bridge of spirits  the devs at ember lab put together an  absolutely gorgeous trailer that  generated plenty of hype almost  immediately  kana is a third-person action-adventure  game that instantly reminded gamers of  something like zelda  this makes even more sense when you  consider imber lab put together a 2016  majora's mask  fan film called terrible fate check it  out if you haven't seen it it's  incredible i'll link to it down in the  description below kana is expected to be  a shorter title that the devs hope you  can comfortably complete in a weekend  who knows if this will change given the  game's recent delay  i know i'd certainly be happy with an  even longer experience if the devs  choose to go that route  i mean just look at this game it's  gorgeous number three  hogwarts legacy if you've been following  my channel already then this one  shouldn't come as much of a surprise  i pretty much grew up with harry potter  and have been dreaming for the  ultimate hogwarts game for years  avalanche software is the dev behind  this one  not to be confused with avalanche  studios known for the just cause games  there's still a lot we don't know about  hogwarts legacy and if it will be able  to live up to the undoubtedly lofty  expectations for it but what we do know  so far  looks very promising the game was leaked  more than two years ago and was  officially unveiled with a trailer at  sony's ps5 showcase event  i've covered what we know so far about  hogwarts legacy quite extensively on my  channel here so click the interactive  card above if you're looking for more  info  on that one moving on though to number  two  demon souls not gonna lie to you guys it  took me multiple  tries to get into the souls games i  think i deleted demon souls off my ps3  more than once before it finally clicked  and i understood  what all the fuss was about i went on to  play all of the other souls games as  well as securo and consider them to be  among my favorite games of all time from  what we've seen so far it looks like the  devs at blue point have done a  phenomenal job at taking that ps3  classic  and putting a glorious glorious fresh  coat of paint on it to make it look  absolutely incredible on the ps5 fans of  the original though are even more  excited about the frame rate  and no sony this doesn't mean you're off  the hook for bloodborne and at number  one  we have god of war ragnarok god awarded  something that  few franchises are able to accomplish  and that it took what was an incredibly  popular formula and completely turned it  on its head  and actually succeeded doing it as much  as i appreciate the original god of war  games for what they were there's no  doubt in my mind that the new version is  even better they replace the angry  destroy everything in his path kratos  with someone much  more relatable even for a god the  relatability factor came as a result of  his son atreus  or maybe you remember him as boy  you thought i was gonna spoil it didn't  you nope nope not here not on this  channel  if you have no idea what i'm talking  about hurry up and play god of war  already for real  it wasn't just the story though the  combat upgrades how you move through the  world pretty much  everything was changed from the old  school god of war games  a sequel was inevitable and all we have  so far is the cryptic teaser trailer but  honestly  that's really all we need to get hyped  for a new god of war  that's gonna be it for today's video as  always thank you guys so much for  watching i'll talk to you again soon

